    "summary": "The remembrance poppy comes from John McCrae's poem In Flanders Fields (3 May 1915), about poppies growing among war graves in Belgium. Moina Michael vowed on 9 November 1918 to wear a red poppy and campaigned for it; Anna Guérin started Poppy Days; Britain's first Poppy Day was 11 November 1921.",
